1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,463
Welcome to ADVISIO.

2
00:00:02,148 --> 00:00:04,598
This walkthrough introduces the Dean
workspace:

3
00:00:04,969 --> 00:00:08,916
college research monitoring, faculty
coordination, document review,

4
00:00:09,091 --> 00:00:10,577
and administrative oversight.

5
00:00:11,169 --> 00:00:13,862
We will follow fictional college
records through the screens and

6
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:16,114
actions available to an authorized
dean.

7
00:00:16,614 --> 00:00:19,261
Your assigned college and account
permissions determine which

8
00:00:19,330 --> 00:00:20,805
records you can access.

9
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:24,163
Sign in using your authorized
institutional account.

10
00:00:24,593 --> 00:00:27,658
Enter your email and password, then
select Sign In.

11
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:31,501
If your account has more than one
workspace, choose Dean.

12
00:00:32,186 --> 00:00:35,077
The workspace identifies your role and
college scope.

13
00:00:35,669 --> 00:00:39,187
This demonstration uses a fictional
dean account, with no access to

14
00:00:39,280 --> 00:00:40,534
real student records.

15
00:00:41,133 --> 00:00:44,094
The Overview brings together the
college research totals.

16
00:00:44,686 --> 00:00:48,087
The four cards show student
researchers, research groups, groups

17
00:00:48,134 --> 00:00:50,816
on track, and groups marked as high
risk.

18
00:00:51,408 --> 00:00:54,496
The sidebar connects the monitoring
and administration areas.

19
00:00:55,088 --> 00:00:59,001
Below the cards, Research Program
Overview compares participation

20
00:00:59,070 --> 00:01:01,404
and workflow progress across programs.

21
00:01:01,903 --> 00:01:05,049
Research Pipeline groups projects by
their current milestone.

22
00:01:05,642 --> 00:01:09,263
Needs Dean Attention lists records
with a recorded risk reason,

23
00:01:09,507 --> 00:01:12,584
while Pending Actions summarizes
accounts and assignments awaiting

24
00:01:12,630 --> 00:01:13,455
attention.

25
00:01:14,067 --> 00:01:17,631
Use the academic year and program
filters to focus the dashboard.

26
00:01:18,223 --> 00:01:21,579
Select an academic year, then inspect
the updated research

27
00:01:21,613 --> 00:01:22,310
information.

28
00:01:22,902 --> 00:01:25,236
Choose a program to narrow the scope
further.

29
00:01:25,828 --> 00:01:29,160
A filter with no matching projects can
produce an empty result;

30
00:01:29,531 --> 00:01:31,401
it does not mean the records were
deleted.

31
00:01:31,993 --> 00:01:35,197
Return to all academic years and all
programs when you need the

32
00:01:35,232 --> 00:01:36,590
broader college view.

33
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:39,789
Open Students to inspect the
researcher registry.

34
00:01:40,219 --> 00:01:43,655
Search by name, institutional
identifier, or email.

35
00:01:44,247 --> 00:01:47,521
Each row brings together the student's
program, research group,

36
00:01:47,556 --> 00:01:51,329
adviser, current stage, progress, and
account status.

37
00:01:51,759 --> 00:01:54,685
Here, a prepared fictional account is
pending.

38
00:01:55,370 --> 00:01:57,947
Review its details before selecting
Approve.

39
00:01:58,632 --> 00:02:01,105
After the update, the account shows
Active.

40
00:02:01,697 --> 00:02:03,555
Approval changes account access;

41
00:02:03,927 --> 00:02:07,758
it does not automatically create a
project, assign an adviser, or

42
00:02:07,828 --> 00:02:09,615
complete research requirements.

43
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:14,275
Research Groups lists project titles,
programs, assigned advisers,

44
00:02:14,391 --> 00:02:16,446
current stages, and progress.

45
00:02:17,131 --> 00:02:21,090
Open Progress and Risk for a closer
look, then select High risk.

46
00:02:21,775 --> 00:02:25,084
The example identifies a project with
no recent activity and

47
00:02:25,130 --> 00:02:26,756
displays the recorded reason.

48
00:02:27,348 --> 00:02:30,215
Use that context when deciding what
needs follow-up with the

49
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:31,655
coordinator or adviser.

50
00:02:32,247 --> 00:02:35,115
These indicators describe the recorded
research activity.

51
00:02:35,614 --> 00:02:39,120
They are monitoring signals, rather
than academic grades or a final

52
00:02:39,190 --> 00:02:40,757
judgment about the research.

53
00:02:41,367 --> 00:02:44,560
Faculty Access shows invitations and
access requests.

54
00:02:45,152 --> 00:02:48,832
Select Invite or request access, then
enter the faculty member's

55
00:02:48,879 --> 00:02:52,524
identity, institutional identifier,
and requested roles.

56
00:02:53,116 --> 00:02:56,565
The dean must verify eligibility and
record the basis for that

57
00:02:56,623 --> 00:02:57,505
verification.

58
00:02:58,097 --> 00:03:01,383
Adviser invitations and requests for
Professor Coordinator or

59
00:03:01,464 --> 00:03:04,506
Panelist access follow different
approval paths.

60
00:03:05,005 --> 00:03:07,919
This example submits a Professor
Coordinator request.

61
00:03:08,349 --> 00:03:11,367
Its recorded status is awaiting
administrator approval;

62
00:03:11,796 --> 00:03:14,803
the request itself has not granted the
faculty role.

63
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:18,848
The Advisers screen shows each
adviser's program, active group

64
00:03:18,918 --> 00:03:22,958
count, capacity, available slots, and
groups needing attention.

65
00:03:23,457 --> 00:03:27,045
Invite adviser opens Faculty Access
for the invitation process.

66
00:03:27,474 --> 00:03:31,282
For an existing adviser, select Edit
to review the assigned program,

67
00:03:31,491 --> 00:03:34,870
maximum active groups, and
availability for new requests.

68
00:03:35,671 --> 00:03:38,457
Record a reason before saving a
capacity change.

69
00:03:39,049 --> 00:03:41,963
Changing capacity does not reassign
existing groups.

70
00:03:42,393 --> 00:03:46,189
The updated card shows the new limit
alongside the current workload.

71
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:49,308
In Inbox, select Signature requests.

72
00:03:49,807 --> 00:03:53,116
Read the requester's message and
review the attached document before

73
00:03:53,162 --> 00:03:54,509
choosing Add signature.

74
00:03:55,008 --> 00:03:58,503
The signing screen supports a saved
signature, drawing, an uploaded

75
00:03:58,549 --> 00:04:00,360
image, or a typed signature.

76
00:04:01,045 --> 00:04:03,727
This example uses a typed
demonstration signature.

77
00:04:04,156 --> 00:04:07,349
Review its placement on the document
and the name and date options.

78
00:04:07,779 --> 00:04:11,401
Confirm your password and the
declaration, then select Confirm and

79
00:04:11,482 --> 00:04:12,040
Sign.

80
00:04:12,725 --> 00:04:15,662
The system saves a separate signed
copy with a verification

81
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:16,243
reference.

82
00:04:16,742 --> 00:04:20,144
Return to the thread to inspect the
Signed status and send a reply

83
00:04:20,213 --> 00:04:21,026
when needed.

84
00:04:21,633 --> 00:04:25,220
Defenses provides college-level
oversight of scheduled sessions.

85
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:29,179
The summary cards identify upcoming
defenses, pending panel

86
00:04:29,238 --> 00:04:33,406
confirmations, rescheduling needs, and
results awaiting release.

87
00:04:34,090 --> 00:04:38,258
Upcoming, Needs Attention, and
Completed provide different views of

88
00:04:38,305 --> 00:04:39,094
those records.

89
00:04:39,593 --> 00:04:43,703
Open View details to inspect a
schedule, venue, required panel,

90
00:04:43,820 --> 00:04:45,073
and preparation checks.

91
00:04:45,665 --> 00:04:49,218
A completed record shows an outcome
only when it has been released.

92
00:04:49,810 --> 00:04:53,328
Unreleased results remain private, and
the oversight screen does not

93
00:04:53,386 --> 00:04:55,999
grant permission to submit a
panelist's scores.

94
00:04:56,600 --> 00:05:00,222
Reports offers Research Progress,
Defense Outcomes, and Adviser

95
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:00,884
Workload.

96
00:05:01,314 --> 00:05:05,273
Select the report, academic year, and
program, then review the

97
00:05:05,319 --> 00:05:06,817
matching preview and summary.

98
00:05:07,246 --> 00:05:09,336
Additional filters depend on the
report.

99
00:05:09,835 --> 00:05:13,539
Export PDF downloads the report for
presentation or reference;

100
00:05:14,224 --> 00:05:17,045
Export CSV provides the tabular data.

101
00:05:17,637 --> 00:05:21,538
Exports include all matching rows, not
only the visible page.

102
00:05:22,037 --> 00:05:25,427
Because records may change after the
preview was generated, check

103
00:05:25,485 --> 00:05:28,968
the selected filters and export time
when sharing a report.

104
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:32,317
Announcements lets the dean publish a
message to the assigned

105
00:05:32,363 --> 00:05:34,209
college or a selected program.

106
00:05:34,708 --> 00:05:37,982
Choose the audience first, then enter
the title and message.

107
00:05:38,412 --> 00:05:41,164
Review the recipients and wording
before selecting Publish

108
00:05:41,210 --> 00:05:41,837
announcement.

109
00:05:42,429 --> 00:05:46,028
Here, the action affects only
fictional accounts in the isolated

110
00:05:46,063 --> 00:05:47,410
demonstration workspace.

111
00:05:48,002 --> 00:05:51,218
The confirmation reports the audience
count, and the new message

112
00:05:51,241 --> 00:05:52,959
appears under Current announcements.

113
00:05:53,644 --> 00:05:56,872
That feed also provides a dated record
of previously published

114
00:05:56,918 --> 00:05:57,743
updates.

115
00:05:58,367 --> 00:06:01,200
The Calendar brings together the
research activities available

116
00:06:01,223 --> 00:06:02,105
within your scope.

117
00:06:02,605 --> 00:06:05,890
The month view and Upcoming events
list show dates for defenses,

118
00:06:05,983 --> 00:06:09,536
consultations, deadlines, and other
recorded activities.

119
00:06:10,221 --> 00:06:13,413
Select the prepared college research
review to inspect its time,

120
00:06:13,529 --> 00:06:15,143
location, and description.

121
00:06:15,735 --> 00:06:17,860
The calendar displays Philippine time.

122
00:06:18,359 --> 00:06:22,318
It reflects the schedules recorded in
ADVISIO, so confirm event

123
00:06:22,364 --> 00:06:25,174
details and changes with the
responsible organizer when

124
00:06:25,232 --> 00:06:26,648
coordinating attendance.

125
00:06:27,267 --> 00:06:30,367
Manuscript Reviews lists versions
explicitly assigned to your

126
00:06:30,402 --> 00:06:30,889
account.

127
00:06:31,481 --> 00:06:34,639
Review and decide opens the frozen
document beside the review

128
00:06:34,697 --> 00:06:35,382
controls.

129
00:06:35,882 --> 00:06:39,248
For a manuscript linked to a
requirement submission, the workspace

130
00:06:39,295 --> 00:06:41,094
also includes shared comments.

131
00:06:41,593 --> 00:06:45,831
Select a passage in a text-based PDF
to attach a comment, or refer

132
00:06:45,912 --> 00:06:48,257
to a page when text selection is
unavailable.

133
00:06:48,850 --> 00:06:51,543
Comments and permanent decisions are
separate actions.

134
00:06:51,973 --> 00:06:54,701
This demonstration inspects the record
without submitting a

135
00:06:54,759 --> 00:06:55,920
permanent decision.

136
00:06:56,500 --> 00:06:59,890
Official Copies provides the archived
documents available under your

137
00:06:59,925 --> 00:07:00,993
account's permissions.

138
00:07:01,492 --> 00:07:05,115
Select the authorized project, then
inspect the document title,

139
00:07:05,266 --> 00:07:09,410
archival status, source version,
finalization details, and

140
00:07:09,468 --> 00:07:10,815
verification reference.

141
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:13,857
Open or download a copy for reference.

142
00:07:14,542 --> 00:07:17,596
Verify integrity checks the stored
file against its recorded

143
00:07:17,630 --> 00:07:18,292
checksum.

144
00:07:18,977 --> 00:07:22,228
The archived original is preserved
separately from any visually

145
00:07:22,286 --> 00:07:23,157
signed copy.

146
00:07:23,749 --> 00:07:26,918
Available signing or revocation
controls depend on the role and

147
00:07:26,977 --> 00:07:28,126
document state.

148
00:07:28,733 --> 00:07:31,844
That concludes the ADVISIO Dean
workspace walkthrough.

149
00:07:32,529 --> 00:07:35,896
Return to Overview to review the
college summary, or revisit a

150
00:07:35,954 --> 00:07:37,661
section for its detailed records.

151
00:07:38,253 --> 00:07:41,481
These tools bring research monitoring,
faculty coordination,

152
00:07:41,655 --> 00:07:44,975
document review, and administrative
oversight together in one

153
00:07:45,010 --> 00:07:45,916
workspace.
